<title>USA: Daimler-Benz unit files for $1.0 mln debt.</title>
<headline>Daimler-Benz unit files for $1.0 mln debt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daimler-Benz Vehicle Receivables Corp, a unit of Mercedes-Benz Credit Corp, filed Tuesday with the Securities and Exchange Commission for $1.0 million in Class A asset-backed certificates.</p>
<p>Daimler-Benz Vehicle is a unit of Mercedes-Benz Credit Corp, which in turn is a unit of Daimler-Benz North America Corp, the U.S. subsidiary of Daimler-Benz.</p>
<p>The offering will be made through Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co.</p>
<p>The certificates to be offered represent interest in Daimler-Benz Vehicle Trust 1996-A.</p>
</text>
